      <!-- SECTION 4: Common JSON Syntax Errors -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight">
          Common JSON Syntax Errors
        </h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed">
          Because JSON is derived from JavaScript object syntax, developers frequently make assumptions based on JavaScript's looser syntax rules. Below are the four most frequent JSON mistakes:
        </p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 my-6">
          
          <!-- Error 1: Missing Commas -->
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 space-y-2">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="text-rose-600 dark:text-rose-400 font-bold text-base">✕</span>
              <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Missing Commas</h3>
            </div>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
              A comma is required between every key-value property and array member. Omitting a comma between keys produces a syntax error.
            </p>
            <div class="rounded-lg bg-slate-950 p-3 text-xs font-mono text-rose-300 overflow-x-auto">
              <code>&#123;<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;"name": "John"<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;"age": 30<br />&#125;</code>
            </div>
            <p class="text-[11px] text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 font-medium">
              Fix: Place a comma after <code>"John",</code> to separate properties.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Error 2: Single Quotes -->
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 space-y-2">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="text-rose-600 dark:text-rose-400 font-bold text-base">✕</span>
              <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Single Quotes Instead of Double</h3>
            </div>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
              In JavaScript and Python, single quotes are valid for strings. In standard JSON, all keys and string values must strictly use double quotes.
            </p>
            <div class="rounded-lg bg-slate-950 p-3 text-xs font-mono text-rose-300 overflow-x-auto">
              <code>&#123; 'status': 'active' &#125;</code>
            </div>
            <p class="text-[11px] text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 font-medium">
              Fix: Replace single quotes with standard double quotes: <code>&#123; "status": "active" &#125;</code>.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Error 3: Trailing Commas -->
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 space-y-2">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="text-rose-600 dark:text-rose-400 font-bold text-base">✕</span>
              <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Trailing Commas</h3>
            </div>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
              Placing a comma after the last property or array item is valid in modern ECMAScript, but completely invalid in standard JSON.
            </p>
            <div class="rounded-lg bg-slate-950 p-3 text-xs font-mono text-rose-300 overflow-x-auto">
              <code>&#123;<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;"name": "John",<br />&#125;</code>
            </div>
            <p class="text-[11px] text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 font-medium">
              Fix: Delete the trailing comma after the final property.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Error 4: Unclosed Brackets -->
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 space-y-2">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="text-rose-600 dark:text-rose-400 font-bold text-base">✕</span>
              <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Unclosed Brackets &amp; Braces</h3>
            </div>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
              Every opening brace <code>&#123;</code> must have a matching closing brace <code>&#125;</code>, and every opening bracket <code>[</code> must match a closing <code>]</code>.
            </p>
            <div class="rounded-lg bg-slate-950 p-3 text-xs font-mono text-rose-300 overflow-x-auto">
              <code>&#123; "items": [ "alpha", "beta" &#125;</code>
            </div>
            <p class="text-[11px] text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 font-medium">
              Fix: Ensure brackets are correctly balanced: <code>&#123; "items": [ "alpha", "beta" ] &#125;</code>.
            </p>
          </div>

        </div>
      </section>

